@startuml
title Institutional Onboarding - Enriched Architecture Flow

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

' ==== ENTRY ====
package "1. Client / Sales" {
  [1. Mandate Awarded (SFDC)] as SFDC
}

' ==== ORCHESTRATION ====
package "2. Orchestration (CAM / Workflow)" {
  [2. Initiate Onboarding & Assign CAM] as CAM
}

' ==== EXECUTION ====
package "3. Parallel Execution" {

  package "3A. Compliance" {
    [3.1 KYC / AML (Appway)] as KYC
    [3.2 Risk Approval] as RISK
  }

  package "3B. Legal" {
    [3.3 IMA Negotiation (Compose)] as IMA
    [3.4 Clause Library] as CLAUSE
  }

  package "3C. Operations" {
    [3.5 Account Setup (PANDA)] as ACCOUNT
    [3.6 Guidelines Setup (Beacon)] as GUIDELINES
  }

  package "3D. Supporting" {
    [3.7 Fee Setup (Revport)] as FEE
    [3.8 Reporting Setup (Synopsis)] as REPORT
  }
}

' ==== CONTROL GATE ====
package "4. Control Gate" {
  [4. IMA Sign-Off] as SIGNOFF
}

' ==== COMPLETION ====
package "5. Completion" {
  [5.1 Account Ready] as READY
  [5.2 Initial Funding] as FUNDING
  [5.3 Onboarding Complete (CRM Updated)] as COMPLETE
  [5.4 Post-Onboarding Review] as REVIEW
}

' ==== FLOW ====
SFDC --> CAM

CAM --> KYC
CAM --> IMA
CAM --> ACCOUNT

KYC --> RISK
RISK --> SIGNOFF

IMA --> CLAUSE
CLAUSE --> SIGNOFF

ACCOUNT --> GUIDELINES
GUIDELINES --> SIGNOFF

SIGNOFF --> FEE
SIGNOFF --> REPORT

SIGNOFF --> READY

READY --> FUNDING
FUNDING --> COMPLETE
COMPLETE --> REVIEW

' ==== ENRICHED NOTES ====

note right of CAM
(2) CENTRAL ORCHESTRATION PROBLEM

- CAM coordinates across multiple stakeholders:
  CAM, CARM, CPM, KYC, Legal, PD, Ops, Fee Billing

- No unified workflow tool today
- Manual tracking via emails / checklists

→ Leads to lack of visibility and delays
→ Target: centralized workflow orchestration layer
end note

note right of KYC
(3.1) COMPLIANCE CHALLENGES

- AML / KYC processes are complex and time-consuming
- Heavy manual validation and document collection
- No consistent global process

→ Key contributor to onboarding delays
end note

note right of IMA
(3.3) LEGAL / IMA BOTTLENECK

- IMA negotiation is fragmented
- Back-and-forth between Legal, Sales, Client
- Lack of standardized clause usage

→ Major delay driver in onboarding

→ Target:
- Clause library
- Negotiation workflow
- Approval & escalation automation
end note

note right of ACCOUNT
(3.5) OPERATIONS COMPLEXITY

- Account setup ownership split between CAM & Product Delivery
- Dependencies on multiple downstream setups

→ Lack of clarity causes delays and rework
end note

note right of SIGNOFF
(4) CRITICAL CONTROL GATE

- IMA must be signed before funding
- Dependencies from Compliance, Legal, Ops converge here

→ No real-time tracking of readiness across systems
→ High coordination overhead

→ This is the key bottleneck checkpoint
end note

note bottom
GLOBAL PROBLEM STATEMENT

- Disconnected systems (Appway, PANDA, Revport, etc.)
- Duplicate data entry across platforms
- No golden source of truth
- No consistent unique identifier (e.g. EPI not fully leveraged)
- Limited real-time reporting / MIS

→ Results in inefficiency, errors, and poor client experience

TARGET STATE VISION

- Unified onboarding workflow layer
- Golden source data model
- Integrated systems with real-time updates
- End-to-end visibility and tracking
end note

@enduml